# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# winoracle "null N" mode, N = 0..11, one process each (x64 == x86). A line
# "about: X" with no result line means the call faulted (access violation)
# on Windows. Verdicts vs Vitreo:
#  CheckFormatSupport(*, NULL), CheckFeatureSupport(*, NULL, size),
#  CheckCounterInfo(NULL), GetImmediateContext(NULL): fault on Windows;
#    Vitreo returns E_INVALIDARG / returns. Not a defect (no caller can
#    depend on the fault).
#  CheckMultisampleQualityLevels(.., NULL), CheckCounter(NULL desc),
#  CreateCounter(NULL desc): E_INVALIDARG on both.                correct
#  CheckMultisampleQualityLevels(28, 0, &q): WIN E_FAIL q=0;
#    VIT E_INVALIDARG, q untouched.                               WRONG
